preConditionHook:
// EL: PositionProfit(1) > 0 or TotalTrades = 0.
// Brooks: a breakout trade that came out profitable is itself a sign the trend
// is strong. Both accessors are measured (the `positionprofit`/`totaltrades`
// register row): PositionProfit(1) is the MOST RECENTLY CLOSED position, net of
// the full round turn, and it does not slide while a position is open;
// TotalTrades ticks on the exit's fill bar. The no-trades-yet branch follows
// LastTradeCooldown so the rule does not block the backtest's first entry.
// Unlike LastTradeCooldown there is no BarsSinceExit leg, so after a loss this
// never passes again until a winner closes.
// EL evaluates the whole OR every bar (no short-circuit), but both terms are
// stateless accessor reads, so C++ short-circuiting cannot diverge.
lastWasWinner = el_gt(ctx.PositionProfit(1), 0.0) || ctx.TotalTrades() == 0;
